00:18:22.940 --> 00:18:28.120
with it or anything. And what's funny is, is that you have, you have...

00:18:28.120 --> 00:18:31.500
It sounded really like I'm just like, you really don't want to pay a compliment to this game.

00:18:31.760 --> 00:18:36.120
No, this game is good for the time it came out, but...

00:18:36.720 --> 00:18:40.740
They mentioned, and by they I mean Namco mentioned that when they were developing this game,

00:18:40.740 --> 00:18:43.680
they were taking a look at all successful arcade games at that point.

00:18:44.320 --> 00:18:50.120
And Pac-Man had just come out the year before, but they really liked the little interludes

00:18:50.120 --> 00:18:52.080
that happened between the levels, you know.

00:18:53.480 --> 00:18:57.400
They're like the first cut scenes of video games, if you'll call them that.

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:04.540
But with Galaga, what's interesting is they took that idea of like, oh, an in-between thing,

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:06.400
but just made an in-between level.

00:19:06.400 --> 00:19:08.860
Like, that wasn't done yet.

00:19:09.040 --> 00:19:13.100
The idea of like a break from the gameplay loop to do something different.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:19.500
And I think you can definitely see it in games like Balloon Fight Again, where they added

00:19:19.500 --> 00:19:22.960
in that extra thing where you just had to pop all the balloons like a challenge stage.

00:19:22.980 --> 00:19:25.600
You can see the Galaga effect happening there.

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:32.540
And I guess you can just, you can extrapolate that forward and give any like mini game for

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:35.960
hacking or mini game for lock picking.

00:19:36.160 --> 00:19:37.620
Just that's the Galaga effect.

00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:43.060
Yeah. I mean, you could even say that anything you do between breakfast, lunch, and dinner is

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:48.060
really just a result of Galaga having this challenge mode in it.

00:19:49.340 --> 00:19:53.340
Yeah. Or like there's Kingdom Hearts 1 and then there's Kingdom Hearts 2, but in between there was

00:19:53.340 --> 00:19:54.440
Kingdom Hearts Chain of Memories.

00:19:54.440 --> 00:19:55.340
Kingdom Hearts 1 and then there's Kingdom Hearts 2, but in between there's Kingdom Hearts 2 and

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:57.580
that's like, which is Galaga challenge mode.

00:19:57.820 --> 00:20:05.520
